405
00:19:53,519 --> 00:19:54,880
I, the 1.87-meter genius,

406
00:19:54,880 --> 00:19:55,240
am standing right here.

407
00:19:55,240 --> 00:19:56,279
Can't you see?

408
00:19:56,279 --> 00:19:57,519
Are you talking about yourself?

409
00:20:00,960 --> 00:20:02,559
Didn't I convince you

410
00:20:02,559 --> 00:20:04,119
in that one-on-one?

411
00:20:04,119 --> 00:20:05,160
Want to try again?

412
00:20:05,599 --> 00:20:06,200
No, no, no.

413
00:20:06,200 --> 00:20:06,400
No need.

414
00:20:06,400 --> 00:20:07,240
I'm convinced, I'm convinced.

415
00:20:08,240 --> 00:20:09,480
That's more like it.

416
00:20:10,400 --> 00:20:11,240
But coach,

417
00:20:11,240 --> 00:20:12,400
shouldn't we

418
00:20:12,400 --> 00:20:14,079
learn more about the player

419
00:20:14,319 --> 00:20:15,960
to better handle the game?

420
00:20:16,279 --> 00:20:17,039
Fu Binyan,

421
00:20:17,359 --> 00:20:18,799
do you have more information on him?

422
00:20:19,880 --> 00:20:20,519
No.

423
00:20:22,680 --> 00:20:24,079
Then how can that be?

424
00:20:24,519 --> 00:20:25,960
We need a game guide.

425
00:20:28,880 --> 00:20:30,359
I, the genius coach,

426
00:20:30,359 --> 00:20:32,279
have already planned everything for you.

427
00:20:33,000 --> 00:20:33,920
What?

428
00:20:48,720 --> 00:20:49,480
This is what you and the coach

429
00:20:49,480 --> 00:20:50,279
